    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get that it's hard to predict perfectly, but even the mainstream economists are saying the labor shortage alone would be catastrophic. Like, if you suddenly pull millions of workers out of the workforce, how can anyone say that won't lead to a massive recession or something worse? It seems like the \"growth\" argument is kind of a stretch when the immediate impact is so destructive.",
